.TH EMERALD.CONF 5 "2026-09-07" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
@PROJECT_NAME@.conf \- Emerald build and runtime configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/@PROJECT_NAME@.conf
is sourced as a POSIX shell file by Emerald. Assignments may override build flags, cache locations, package handling, and cleanup behavior. Values are commonly written as shell strings such as \fByes\fR or \fBno\fR.
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
.B SOURCE_DIR
Source cache directory. Default is the configured cache directory followed by \fBsources\fR.
.TP
.B PACKAGE_DIR
Built-package cache directory. Default is the configured cache directory followed by \fBpackages\fR.
.TP
.B WORK_DIR
Temporary build directory. Default is the configured cache directory followed by \fBwork\fR.
.TP
.B CURL_OPTS
Additional options passed to curl when fetching sources.
.TP
.B COMPRESSION_MODE
Package compression method, normally \fBxz\fR.
.TP
.B NO_STRIP
Set to \fByes\fR to disable stripping binaries.
.TP
.B IGNORE_CHECKSUM
Set to \fByes\fR to skip source checksum verification.
.TP
.B KEEP_DOC, KEEP_LIBTOOL, KEEP_LOCALE, KEEP_MAN, KEEP_INFO, KEEP_HELP
Set to \fByes\fR to retain the corresponding files during packaging. The default policy is defined by the installed template.
.TP
.B NOCOLOR
Set to \fByes\fR to disable colored output.
.TP
.B CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, FCFLAGS, FFLAGS, LDFLAGS, MAKEFLAGS
Compiler, linker, and parallel-build settings exported to build scripts.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
COMPRESSION_MODE="xz"
KEEP_DOC="yes"
KEEP_MAN="yes"
NOCOLOR="yes"
.fi
.SH SECURITY
This file is executed by the shell. Only trusted administrators should edit it; do not place untrusted input in assignments or command substitutions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR @PROJECT_NAME@ (1),
.BR pkgbuild (1)
